WEBVTT


00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.210
June 3, 3616.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.000
I'm Nameless.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:10.050
I can no longer remember my real name.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.890
June 7, 3616.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:20.350
There are other children
named Nameless like me.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.390
Almost all of them have lifeless eyes.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.600
In this situation,

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.400
I've found a few people I can talk to.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:31.690
Is this what it feels like
to have friends?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.950
If we can get out of here,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.040
the three of us will form a party.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.210
Being adventurers sounds nice.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.040
Teacher, where are we going?

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.460
Our destination is west of Alessa,

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:50.920
Port Dars.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.300
Urushi, head straight west!

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.510
Port…

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.720
Delicious fish.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.010
I can't wait.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.810
Hey, you're going too fast.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.180
As expected, he's out of mana.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.520
Good work, Urushi.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.730
Go rest in the shadow.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.240
We're not in a hurry, so let's eat first.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.700
Curry?

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:20.200
This time,
it's my special vegetable curry.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:26.670
- Curry…
- All right. Wipe your drool.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.770
(Reincarnated as a Sword Season 2)

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.340
Ta-da!

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.390
Finished.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.390
I'm so happy.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.810
Teacher, I want another bowl.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.560
(Episode 1: The Island Floating in the Sky)

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.060
(Episode 1: The Island Floating in the Sky)
By the way, we're quite far from Alessa now.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.110
What's that?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.400
That's a floating island.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.570
So it's an island?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.870
Sometimes, they float in the sky.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.620
When I was a slave,

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.740
looking for that was my only joy.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.540
Your only joy?

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.590
Can't we use
Urushi's Midair Jump to get there?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.800
Will his mana run out?

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.300
Let's use Levitation Skill.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:44.850
That's strange.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:45.890
It stopped.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.930
There's a height limit.
We can't go any higher.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:50.980
I see.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.850
Thank you, Ms. Announcer.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:56.060
Then I'll use Telekinesis
to get there by myself.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.480
It's not fair, Teacher.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.320
I want to go too.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.740
Fair enough.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.910
I'll secure Fran's feet with Telekinesis.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.120
Urushi, get in the shadow.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.460
All right. Let's go!

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.710
Telekinesis Midair Slide!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.300
As expected of Fran.
Her sense of balance is superb!

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.470
Let's keep this momentum and head over!

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.140
The floating island!

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:28.810
What's wrong?

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:30.680
Teacher.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.980
Something is coming.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.310
A skeleton?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.560
Are they the Undead?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.900
I don't think they're here to welcome us.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.530
Fine by me.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.160
How can they hit us from there?

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.370
Fran!

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.660
Fire Arrow!

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.000
What? This fellow…

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.040
Appraisal!

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.000
(Legendary Skeleton Dark Knight)

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.250
(Race: Beast, Undead)
Its magic defense

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.290
(Status: Guardian, Undead, Level 24)
and melee skills

00:04:58.380 --> 00:04:59.380
(Special Skill: Potential Release)
surpass

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.460
(Title: Dungeon Guardian)
a Greater Demon's!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:02.800
Fran!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.840
Maintaining Midair Slide
is taking all I've got.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:05.930
I know.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:06.840
Here it comes!

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.300
Dimensional Storage.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.310
This is the sword I took

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:12.320
(Shadowsteel Long Sword)
from the Greater Demon.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.680
(Shadowsteel Long Sword)
Go!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.520
I hate having her use
any sword other than me.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:21.980
What?

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.570
(Magic Sword: Death Gaze)
A magic sword?

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.740
(Skill: Instant Death)
A low chance to trigger instant death.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.490
Instant death?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.200
Urushi, can you go?

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.620
Teacher, you're still the easiest to use.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.250
Of course I am.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:40.710
Let's go.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.050
Teacher, please provide cover.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.220
Got it! Urushi, you support her too!

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.760
Fire Blast!

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:57.940
He blocked it.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.980
Midair Jump.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.150
Go, Fran!

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.400
Dragon Fang!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.160
It worked.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:14.120
Urushi, a foothold!

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:16.830
Are you out of mana?

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.210
Get back into the shadow.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.380
Then I'll use my Telekinesis Midair Slide.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.550
I'm out of mana too.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.550
I'll win next time.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.100
It hasn't chased us since then.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.100
A Dungeon Guardian?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.230
This is so frustrating!

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.480
Damn it.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.270
I'll remember this!

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.360
By the way, what do we do now?

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.280
We're falling.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.080
Use Midair Jump to cushion the impact.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.200
Okay.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.250
Midair Jump!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.160
It's no use.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.830
No…

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.920
In that case,
keep casting it until your mana is gone.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.880
Roger!

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.130
There's a house all the way out here?

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.430
Teacher.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.470
I'm out of mana.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.100
Fran, are you okay?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.690
My butt hurts.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.950
What is this?

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.950
A field inside a house?

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.410
The soil is so soft.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.330
Can things grow here

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:38.500
(Necro-Grass: Spirit Grass)
without any windows?

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:40.660
Something is there.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:41.870
Be careful.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:49.970
Another skeleton.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.470
Fran, the magic stone is in its torso.

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.550
Okay. One strike and it's over.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.510
Help!

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.350
I don't taste good.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:00.680
Please don't eat me.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:02.640
I won't eat you.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.310
Who is this guy?

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.150
I'm Bernard, a good skeleton.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:11.610
He has a name? Is he a familiar?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:15.320
My master is a great necromancer!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.280
A necromancer?

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.290
That's right.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.290
Who's there?

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:24.000
Do you want to know?

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.790
Then I shall tell you.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.050
The king of the Undead
who lurks in the darkness.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.260
The one who gazes
into the abyss of wisdom.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:35.430
My name is Jean Du Vix.

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:38.140
- How suspicious.
- How suspicious.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:43.980
To think you'd dare trespass into
my Necromancy Research Lab.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.610
It seems you want me to put
that vessel to good use.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.400
Appraise anyone suspicious immediately.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.110
(Special Skill: Soul Eye)
What?

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.030
(Genius Assassin, The Undead Creator)
Well,

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:55.950
(Slaughterer, Necromancer, Undead King)
he's strong.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:56.870
(Jean Du Vix, Age: 49)
He's a demonkin

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.780
(Race: Demonkin, Job: Necromancer)
and

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.700
(Level 45)
a necromancer.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.580
Are demonkin that rare?

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.210
They're rare on this continent,
so it's understandable.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.210
Besides, I'm a necromancer.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.290
We're often considered evil.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.170
But that's a misunderstanding.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.170
But you look so suspicious.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:16.720
Setting that aside,

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:19.430
I'm the victim here.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.520
If the corpses of living creatures
are left unattended,

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.030
they'll be possessed by stray spirits
and become harmful undead.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.990
Before that happens, we control them

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.200
and give them a reason to exist.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:38.370
That's what we necromancers do.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.700
It's not evil but a noble profession.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.960
Welcome to my Necromancy Research Lab

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.630
of Infinite Darkness
and the Abyss of Death.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.670
He talks a big game, but…

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:54.170
It's so ordinary.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.340
To prevent danger from spreading,

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:59.510
the main part of the lab
is deep underground.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:03.180
Indeed, I sense an eerie mana
coming from below.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.520
Please have some tea.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:06.640
Thank you.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.520
(Necro-Tea: Affects the Soul)
Well,

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.650
(Has a Calming Effect)
let's see.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.110
Despite its look, it seems harmless.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.030
But it tastes terrible.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.700
I see.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.870
So that's why you fell.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.540
Bernard, report on the field damage.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.130
About 30 percent is ruined.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.050
Those are Grade 1 Necro-Grass used for

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:37.090
making Necro-Potions
and as mediums for necromancy.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:41.430
If the living touch them, they're tainted
by vitality and become useless.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.970
I recall Randell's shop
sells Grade 3 Necro-Potions.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.060
But they cost 300,000 gold coins.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:49.900
Is that expensive?

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.900
I didn't grow them for money.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:56.820
Let me think.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:00.910
In that case, I'd like you
to grant me a favor in return.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.410
A favor?

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.280
But before that…

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.700
It's about time you spoke up.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.210
Intelligence Weapon.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.120
What?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.960
My special skill, Soul Eye,

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.920
allows me to see skills engraved on souls.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.760
Blocking Appraisal is useless.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.350
Teacher, what should we do?

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:25.010
It can't be helped.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:28.600
As you suspected, I'm Fran's sword.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.190
You're communicating with Telepathy.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.900
And what an outstanding performance.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.030
That's right.
Teacher is a super strong sword.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.400
His name is Teacher.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.860
Teacher?

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.910
That's an odd name for a magic sword.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.500
So what's your request?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.710
If you want to study Fran's corpse
or borrow me,

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:52.790
I'm going to refuse.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.880
I'm not interested in that.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.590
I have high hopes for your abilities.

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:03.430
I'd like you to help me
conquer the dungeon.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.180
I knew it.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.470
It's the floating island, right?

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:13.810
As expected of an Intelligence Weapon.
You're quite sharp.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:18.230
Because that Skeleton Knight's title
was Dungeon Guardian.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.110
In the center of the floating island,

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.610
there's a dungeon that only I know about.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:28.410
This story begins ten years ago.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:30.910
Wait. Is this going to take long?

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.660
If it's too long, Fran will fall asleep.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.250
Please keep it brief.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:35.330
Teacher.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.300
I'm already a D-rank adventurer.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:42.260
Even if it's long, I can listen to it all.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.720
I see.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:44.680
Sorry.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:47.350
I shouldn't keep treating you
like a child.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.220
Then I'll continue.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.230
Back then, in order to reach

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:54.980
a higher level as a necromancer

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:57.400
-and to master new spells…
-Fran fell asleep instantly.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.440
So I'll keep it short.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:04.860
It's said that this incident began
in this desolate region

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.450
with reports of undead sightings,

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.740
usually found in battlefields
and graveyards.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.120
As a result of Jean's investigation,

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.870
he discovered that
among the large rocks and plants,

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:16.290
there was an accumulation
of undead-attribute mana.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.710
He wanted to find out
where the undead came from.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:22.710
They were actually rubble and debris
from the floating island.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.550
To confirm this,

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:30.560
I went to explore the dungeon
on the floating island a few years ago.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:34.060
The dungeon is a den of undead beasts.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:38.060
And while I was there,
I was attacked by a powerful beast.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:41.610
While my familiar, Steven, held it back,

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.360
I barely managed to escape.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.400
A powerful beast?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.110
An Undead Devourer.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:52.700
It's a B-rank threat, an undead
that devours other undead.

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.960
A B-rank threat…

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.080
There's something like that
besides the Skeleton Knight?

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.500
The Necro-Grass was meant
to help defeat those undead.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.260
I'd like you to take the place
of that item.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:08.390
Is that too much of a burden?

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.050
No problem.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.640
We may not look it,
but we're D-rank adventurers.

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:16.730
You're from the Alessa Guild, right?

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.020
You knew?

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:20.310
I'm an adventurer myself after all.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.320
Are you, Jean?

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.940
That's surprising.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.400
I may not look it,
but I'm a B-rank adventurer.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:27.950
Silver.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.280
So cool!

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.910
Though I was given the infamous
nickname Jean the Slayer…

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.250
That's a scary nickname.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.920
I know, right?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.880
All I did during the war
with the Raydoss Kingdom

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.960
was turn the unconscious enemies
into undead and control them,

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.920
and then lead them in a massive attack.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:48.050
That's still pretty outrageous.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.300
Anyway, this is my request.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.180
Naturally, I'll pay you as well.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.260
What do you think?

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.270
We're the ones in the wrong here.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.100
I'm happy to go to the dungeon.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.310
Besides…

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.730
You mean that Skeleton Knight, right?

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:07.150
I'm definitely going to get
my revenge on that guy.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.610
Then it's settled.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:11.030
Jean, we'll take the job.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:13.780
You'll leave tomorrow.

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:16.660
Stay at my lab tonight.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.080
We're staying here?

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.130
Behold.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.090
The essence of my necromancy.

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.470
Break free from the cycle
of the underworld

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.470
and accept a fleeting life.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:38.350
Shatter the shackles of the abyss
before me now!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:42.190
Summon Overspec Undead!

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:47.570
I shall grant you a name.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.990
You're Andy.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.660
So this is what
a professional summoning looks like.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:00.210
We'll fly to the floating island on Andy.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.170
Hey, are you okay?

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:05.880
Nice to meet you, Andy.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.590
How cute.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.590
Overspec…

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:13.510
(Andy: Undead Beast)
Has he been granted

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.800
(Status: Over-Enhanced Undead Familiar)
more power than usual?

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:16.310
(Overspec Skeleton Wyvern)
He's much stronger

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.970
(Wraith, Contract, Weakness Mitigation)
than a low-rank wyvern.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.600
Right?

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:22.390
However, in exchange,

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:25.610
he'll vanish within 24 hours.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.020
I see.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:30.110
Unlike Urushi,
he's only for short-term operations.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:33.410
Your familiar, Urushi, is excellent too.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.780
Why don't you just die
so I can try making you overspec?

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:37.780
Rejected.

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.490
Absolutely not!

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.410
What a pity.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:45.460
A necromancer's intuition is dangerous.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.840
You said only you know about the dungeon.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.010
Does that mean the guild doesn't know?

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.430
I suppose so.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.590
After all, I haven't reported it.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.350
Aren't you obligated to report it?

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:01.770
That floating island drifts
between the airspace of Granzell,

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.310
Raydoss to the north,

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:07.400
and the Kingdom of Belioth.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:09.360
It doesn't belong to any one nation.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.530
So I have no obligation to report it.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.490
Is that so?

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.490
As long as we don't get caught.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.280
Bernard.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:19.700
How are Winged Tiger Skeletons?

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.160
Everything is ready.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.160
Winged Tiger Skeletons?

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:26.040
Skeleton decoys used for
defense and distraction.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.710
I see.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:30.340
Our target is
the floating island's dungeon.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:33.130
Now, take flight, Andy!

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.560
Safe travels.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:44.100
How can it fly
when its wings are so battered?

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:47.900
It's a magical beast that
originally relies on its flying skills.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.360
I see.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.900
They're here. Is it the Skeleton Knight?

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:54.820
No.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:57.660
Usually, when a party
approaches the floating island,

00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:59.870
a flock of Bone Birds will attack.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.830
And they've got low-rank wyverns too.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.750
Winged Tiger Skeletons
are already engaged.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.210
There are so many of them.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.420
Fran, Teacher,
please prepare to intercept.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.300
Teacher and I will split up.

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.880
Telekinesis!

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.890
Illusionary Stone Sword!

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:22.970
All right. Let's go!

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.530
Mana Stone Absorption.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.400
Feast to your heart's content.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.200
Hey.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:45.290
Is it coming?

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.960
They even have those things?

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:53.500
Fran!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:55.840
Hey, we've been hit!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.930
Is Andy okay?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:01.760
No, he can't take that many hits.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.560
Everyone, gather around.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:05.350
- What are you doing?
- Urushi.

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:07.430
We're going to charge in all at once.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.350
What?

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.150
Instant Summon.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.310
Undead Slime!

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.780
Get inside the ribcage with the slime.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:17.650
Is this safe?

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.700
I've adjusted it to be harmless.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.410
Andy…

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.460
Are they pursuing us?

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:34.550
Andy!

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:37.340
What are you doing?

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.010
Good work, Andy.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.760
Now, go!

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.390
Ultimate Reverse Breath!

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:49.100
We're breaking through!

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.730
Is that a barrier?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.610
It's no match for Andy!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.940
Don't bite your tongue, Fran!

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.000
Fran, are you okay?

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.670
I'm fine.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.010
Andy…

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.590
You did well.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.640
I see. He has exhausted his mana.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:26.180
Thank you, Andy.

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.970
It was brief,

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:30.020
but I enjoyed the time we spent together.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.480
Andy's flying was amazing.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.610
You were incredible.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.980
At least let me be the one
to send you off.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.240
Your soul fragments

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.990
are finally freed from their resentment.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.490
May you rest in peace.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:47.490
Purify the spirit.

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:51.080
Andy, you did a great job.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:52.410
Bye-bye.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:56.960
Purification Magic
seems to consume a lot of mana.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.510
Even though Andy would have
disappeared on his own,

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.970
Jean used Purification Magic
to send him off.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:06.680
It shows his pride as a necromancer.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:12.520
The road ahead
will be tiring enough to fall apart.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.900
Because he's a skeleton. Get it?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.310
That's a necromancer joke!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:18.980
What does that mean?

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.610
What's wrong with this guy?

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:29.620
August 27, 3616.

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:33.040
I occasionally hear screams
coming from the distance.

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.540
What happened to them?

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.790
Are those two okay?

00:21:38.840 --> 00:21:42.460
August 30, 3616.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.430
I understand why there were screams now.

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.930
We are experimental subjects.

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:55.600
Stop…

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:39.960
(Next Episode: Jean Du Vix Is Excellent)

